---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
const SIZES = [10, 20, 50, 100, 200, 500, 1000, 2000, 5000, 10000, 100000, 1000000, 5000000, 10000000];
const A_CLASSES = [['log', 'O(log n)'], ['n', 'O(n)'], ['nlogn', 'O(n log n)'], ['n2', 'O(n²)']];
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="Pick the input size n and see how many steps each class of algorithm needs. Time is an assumption: one step takes one nanosecond, everything else ignored. Nothing here is timed on your machine.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Set <b>Input size n</b> to <b>1,000,000</b>. O(n) takes 1,000,000 steps, about 1 ms. O(n log n) takes <b>20,000,000</b> steps, 20 ms. O(n²) takes 1,000,000,000,000 steps, which is <b>16.7</b> minutes: the verdict is only "slow, but finishes", and at n = 10,000,000 it turns to "not in practice".</li>
    <li>Set <b>Input size n</b> to <b>50</b>: O(n²) is only <b>2,500</b> steps, over in 2.5 µs, so it is fine. O(2ⁿ) already needs more than a million billion steps. Set <b>Input size n</b> to <b>10</b> and O(n!) is <b>3,628,800</b> steps: harmless, until n grows.</li>
    <li>Under "Give one algorithm a constant factor", set <b>Algorithm A</b> to O(n) with <b>Constant factor</b> <b>100</b> and <b>Algorithm B</b> to O(n²). At n = 50, A costs <b>5,000</b> steps and B only <b>2,500</b>: the better class loses. The crossover is at <b>n = 101</b>.</li>
    <li>Now set <b>Algorithm B</b> to O(n log n): the crossover becomes "never in practice": log₂ n has to pass the factor before O(n log n) costs more than 100 steps per item, and that takes an astronomically large n. The constant factor never goes away, it only stops mattering when the classes are far apart.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg bo" data-bo>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Input size n <select class="pg-in" data-n>{SIZES.map((n) => <option value={n} selected={n === 1000}>{n.toLocaleString('en-US')}</option>)}</select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="bo-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Steps by complexity class">
      <table class="bo-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Class</th><th scope="col">Steps</th><th scope="col">Time at 1 ns per step</th><th scope="col">Verdict</th><th scope="col">Steps, log scale</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody data-rows></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note">The bar is the number of digits of the step count (full bar: 20 digits or more), so each tick to the right is ten times more work. The exact step counts are in the table.</p>
    <h3 class="bo-h">Give one algorithm a constant factor</h3>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Algorithm A <select class="pg-in" data-a>{A_CLASSES.map(([v, t]) => <option value={v} selected={v === 'n'}>{t}</option>)}</select></label>
      <label>Constant factor <select class="pg-in" data-c><option value="1">1</option><option value="10">10</option><option value="100" selected>100</option><option value="1000">1000</option></select></label>
      <label>Algorithm B <select class="pg-in" data-b>{A_CLASSES.map(([v, t]) => <option value={v} selected={v === 'n2'}>{t}</option>)}</select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-boxa><h3>A at this n</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-oa></span><span class="pg-note" data-na></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-boxb><h3>B at this n</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-ob></span><span class="pg-note" data-nb></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Crossover</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-ox></span><span class="pg-note" data-nx></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict role="status"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: a step is one basic operation and takes 1 ns, with no caches, memory or I/O. The log is base 2, rounded up. A has the constant factor (it does that many steps per item), B has none. For 2ⁿ and n! the exact count is shown while it fits in a safe integer, and a power of ten after that. "Fine" is up to 1 second, "slow" up to 1 day, beyond that "not in practice".</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, formatThousands, formatOneDecimalBelow100 } from '../playground';

  interface Cost { exact: number | null; log10: number }
  const NS_PER_S = 1e9;
  const SAFE = Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER;
  const log2c = (n: number) => { let k = 0; for (let p = 1; p < n; p *= 2) k++; return k; };
  const LOG10_2 = Math.log10(2);
  const exactCost = (x: number): Cost => ({ exact: x, log10: Math.log10(x) });
  function factorial(n: number): Cost {
    let x = 1;
    for (let i = 2; i <= n; i++) { x *= i; if (x > SAFE) break; }
    if (x <= SAFE) return exactCost(x);
    return { exact: null, log10: (n * Math.log(n) - n + 0.5 * Math.log(2 * Math.PI * n)) / Math.LN10 }; // Stirling's approximation
  }
  const CLASSES: { id: string; name: string; cost: (n: number) => Cost }[] = [
    { id: '1', name: 'O(1)', cost: () => exactCost(1) },
    { id: 'log', name: 'O(log n)', cost: (n) => exactCost(Math.max(1, log2c(n))) },
    { id: 'n', name: 'O(n)', cost: (n) => exactCost(n) },
    { id: 'nlogn', name: 'O(n log n)', cost: (n) => exactCost(n * Math.max(1, log2c(n))) },
    { id: 'n2', name: 'O(n²)', cost: (n) => exactCost(n * n) },
    { id: '2n', name: 'O(2ⁿ)', cost: (n) => (n <= 52 ? exactCost(2 ** n) : { exact: null, log10: n * LOG10_2 }) },
    { id: 'fact', name: 'O(n!)', cost: factorial },
  ];
  const stepsText = (c: Cost) => (c.exact !== null ? formatThousands(c.exact) : `about 10^${formatThousands(Math.round(c.log10))}`);
  const UNITS: [number, string, string][] = [[1e-6, 'ns', '1e9'], [1e-3, 'µs', '1e6'], [1, 'ms', '1e3']];
  function secondsText(c: Cost): string {
    if (c.exact === null) {
      const yearsLog = c.log10 - 9 - Math.log10(365.25 * 86400);
      return yearsLog > 10.2 ? `about 10^${formatThousands(Math.round(yearsLog))} years, longer than the age of the universe` : `about 10^${Math.round(yearsLog)} years`;
    }
    const s = c.exact / NS_PER_S;
    for (const [limit, unit, mult] of UNITS) if (s < limit) return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(s * Number(mult))} ${unit}`;
    if (s < 60) return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(s)} s`;
    if (s < 3600) return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(s / 60)} minutes`;
    if (s < 86400) return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(s / 3600)} hours`;
    if (s < 365.25 * 86400) return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(s / 86400)} days`;
    return `${formatThousands(Math.round(s / (365.25 * 86400)))} years`;
  }
  const verdictOf = (c: Cost): 'fine' | 'slow' | 'never' => {
    const s = c.log10 - 9;
    return s <= 0 ? 'fine' : s <= Math.log10(86400) ? 'slow' : 'never';
  };
  const VERDICT_TEXT = { fine: 'fine', slow: 'slow, but finishes', never: 'not in practice' };
  const VERDICT_COLOR = { fine: 'var(--good)', slow: 'var(--signal)', never: 'var(--bad)' };

  // Where the cheaper class starts to win: the smallest n from which low (with its constant factor) is cheaper than high.
  const BEYOND = 1e12;
  function crossover(low: (n: number) => number, cLow: number, high: (n: number) => number, cHigh: number): number | null {
    const wins = (n: number) => cLow * low(n) < cHigh * high(n);
    let hi = 1;
    while (!wins(hi)) { hi *= 2; if (hi > BEYOND) return null; }
    let lo = Math.max(1, hi / 2);
    while (hi - lo > 1) { const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi) / 2); if (wins(mid)) hi = mid; else lo = mid; }
    return wins(lo) ? lo : hi;
  }
  const RANK: Record<string, number> = { log: 0, n: 1, nlogn: 2, n2: 3 };
  const costOf = (id: string) => CLASSES.find((c) => c.id === id)!.cost;
  const num = (id: string) => (n: number) => costOf(id)(n).exact as number;

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-bo]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const rows = q('[data-rows]');
    const sel = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    function draw() {
      const n = Number(sel('[data-n]'));
      rows.textContent = '';
      for (const cls of CLASSES) {
        const c = cls.cost(n);
        const v = verdictOf(c);
        const tr = document.createElement('tr');
        const cell = (text: string) => { const td = document.createElement('td'); td.textContent = text; tr.appendChild(td); return td; };
        cell(cls.name); cell(stepsText(c)); cell(secondsText(c));
        const vt = cell(VERDICT_TEXT[v]); vt.style.color = VERDICT_COLOR[v]; vt.style.fontWeight = '600';
        const bar = document.createElement('td');
        const fill = document.createElement('span'); fill.className = 'bo-bar';
        fill.style.width = `${Math.min(100, Math.max(2, (Math.floor(c.log10) + 1) * 5))}%`; fill.style.background = VERDICT_COLOR[v];
        bar.appendChild(fill); tr.appendChild(bar);
        rows.appendChild(tr);
      }
      // The constant-factor control.
      const a = sel('[data-a]'), b = sel('[data-b]'), factor = Number(sel('[data-c]'));
      const fa = num(a), fb = num(b);
      const costA = factor * fa(n), costB = fb(n);
      q('[data-oa]').textContent = formatThousands(costA);
      q('[data-na]').textContent = `${factor} x ${CLASSES.find((c) => c.id === a)!.name} at n = ${formatThousands(n)}`;
      q('[data-ob]').textContent = formatThousands(costB);
      q('[data-nb]').textContent = `${CLASSES.find((c) => c.id === b)!.name} at n = ${formatThousands(n)}`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-boxa]').style.setProperty('--c', costA <= costB ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-boxb]').style.setProperty('--c', costB < costA ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      let ox: string, nx: string;
      if (RANK[a] === RANK[b]) {
        ox = 'none'; nx = factor === 1 ? 'the same class and the same factor: A and B cost the same at every n' : `the same class: A is always ${factor} times more expensive`;
      } else {
        const aLow = RANK[a] < RANK[b];
        const x = aLow ? crossover(fa, factor, fb, 1) : crossover(fb, 1, fa, factor);
        const lowName = CLASSES.find((c) => c.id === (aLow ? a : b))!.name;
        ox = x === null ? 'never in practice' : `n = ${formatThousands(x)}`;
        nx = x === null ? `${lowName} would only get ahead beyond n = 10^12` : `${lowName} is cheaper from this size on, and the other one is cheaper below it`;
      }
      q('[data-ox]').textContent = ox; q('[data-nx]').textContent = nx;
      const ratio = costA >= costB ? costA / costB : costB / costA;
      const verdict = costA === costB ? `At n = ${formatThousands(n)} both cost ${formatThousands(costA)} steps.` : `At n = ${formatThousands(n)}, ${costA < costB ? 'A' : 'B'} is cheaper, by a factor of ${formatOneDecimalBelow100(ratio)}.`;
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = verdict;
    }
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .bo-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .playground .bo-h { margin: 14px 0 4px; font-size: 1rem; }
  .playground .bo-table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .88rem; }
  .playground .bo-table th, .playground .bo-table td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); white-space: nowrap; }
  .playground .bo-table td:nth-child(2), .playground .bo-table td:nth-child(3) { font-family: var(--font-mono); white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere; min-width: 7rem; }
  .playground .bo-table td:last-child { min-width: 120px; width: 28%; }
  .playground .bo-bar { display: block; height: 12px; border-radius: 3px; }
</style>
